 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "In the given figure the <span data-math=\"x\">x</span>-axis on the graph represents the years. The <i>y</i>-axis represents the number of teachers at Jones High School.\n<figure>\n<figcaption>Teachers at Jones High</figcaption>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/6f777fa1633cb21e.png\" alt=\"A graph titled, Teachers at Jones High. The horizontal axis representing years ranges from 1990 to 2025, in increments of 5. The vertical axis representing the number of teachers ranges from 0 to 90, in increments of 10. The graph shows a line that passes through the points, (1990, 20), (1995, 30), (2000, 50), (2005, 50), (2010, 40), (2015, 60), and (2020, 80).\"></figure>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 511321,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Interpret the <span data-math=\"x\">x</span>- and <span data-math=\"y\">y</span>-intercept.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "(0, 20) is the <span data-math=\"y\\text{-intercept}\">y\\text{-intercept}</span> and represents that there were 20 teachers at Jones High School in 1990. There is no <span data-math=\"x\\text{-intercept}\">x\\text{-intercept}</span>."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 511322,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "For each segment, find the slope.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Between 1990 and 1995:</p>\n<p>The rise is 10. The run is 5.</p>\n<p>Use the slope formula. <span data-math=\"m = \\frac{{rise}}{{run}} = \\frac{{10}}{5} = 2\"></span></p>\n<p>On average, the school gained two teachers every year between 1990 and 1995.</p>\n<p>Between 1995 and 2000:</p>\n<p>The rise is 50 – 30 = 20.</p>\n<p>The run is 2000 – 1995 = 5.</p>\n<p>Use the slope formula. <span data-math=\"m = \\frac{{rise}}{{run}} = \\frac{{20}}{5} = 4\"></span></p>\n<p>On average, the school gained four teachers every year between 1995 and 2000.</p>\n<p>Between 2000 and 2005:</p>\n<p>The rise is 0.</p>\n<p>The run is 5.</p>\n<p>The slope is 0.</p>\n<p>On average, the school gained zero teachers every year between 2000 and 2005. That means the number of teachers remained constant.</p>\n<p>Between 2005 and 2010:</p>\n<p>The rise is –10.</p>\n<p>The run is 5.</p>\n<p>Use the slope formula. <span data-math=\"m = \\frac{{rise}}{{run}} = \\frac{{ - 10}}{5} = - 2\"></span></p>\n<p>On average, the school lost two teachers every year between 2005 and 2010.</p>\n<p>Between 2010 and 2015:</p>\n<p>The rise is 20.</p>\n<p>The run is 5.</p>\n<p>Use the slope formula. <span data-math=\"m = \\frac{{rise}}{{run}} = \\frac{{20}}{5} = 4\"></span></p>\n<p>On average, the school gained four teachers every year between 2010 and 2015.</p>\n<p>Between 2015 and 2020:</p>\n<p>The rise is 20.</p>\n<p>The run is 5.</p>\n<p>Use the slope formula. <span data-math=\"m = \\frac{{rise}}{{run}} = \\frac{{20}}{5} = 4\"></span></p>\n<p>On average, the school gained four teachers every year between 2015 and 2020, the same slope as between 2010 and 2015.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "In the first 5 years the slope is 2; this means that on average, the school gained 2 teachers every year between 1990 and 1995. Between 1995 and 2000, the slope is 4; on average the school gained 4 teachers every year. Then the slope is 0 between 2000 and 2005 meaning the number of teachers remained the same. There was a decrease in teachers between 2005 and 2010, represented by a slope of –2. Finally, the slope is 4 between 2010 and 2020, which indicates that on average the school gained 4 teachers every year."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 511323,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Create an interpretation of this graph (i.e., make up a story that goes with it).",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Answers will vary. Jones High School was founded in 1990 and hired 2 teachers per year until 1995, when they had an increase in students and they hired 4 teachers per year for the next 5 years. Then there was a hiring freeze, and no teachers were hired between 2000 and 2005. After the hiring freeze, the student population decreased, and they lost 2 teachers per year until 2010. Another surge in student population meant Jones High School hired 4 new teachers per year until 2020 when they had 80 teachers at the school. "
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
